 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "monsters is a list of rows [label, defeats]. A label is the monster name, followed by \"*\" when the monster is hostile. The rows describe a tree rooted at root: every child name has its own row and appears in exactly one defeat list, and every row is reachable from root. Defeat is transitive: a monster can defeat exactly its strict descendants. Return, sorted in code-point order, the names of the non-hostile monsters whose strict descendants include every hostile monster (with no hostile monster at all, every non-hostile monster qualifies).",
  "provenance": [
